{%- doc -%}
  Print a product price in the unit the shop talks in.

  Cloth is cut in half metres and Shopify cart quantities are whole numbers, so the sold
  unit for anything tagged "Fabric" is half a metre: the variant price is the price of
  0.5 m. Customers think in metres, so every price shown for a fabric is doubled back to
  the metre here, in one place, rather than in each card and section.

  @param {object} product - the product the price belongs to (decides the unit)
  @param {number} [price] - the figure to print, in cents; defaults to product.price
  @param {boolean} [unit] - pass false to leave off the "/ m" suffix (struck prices, totals)
{%- enddoc -%}
{%- liquid
  assign zp_money = price
  if zp_money == blank
    assign zp_money = product.price
  endif
  assign zp_fabric = false
  if product.tags contains 'Fabric'
    assign zp_fabric = true
    assign zp_money = zp_money | times: 2
  endif
-%}
{{- zp_money | money -}}
{%- if zp_fabric and unit != false %} <span class="zp-uom" style="letter-spacing:.02em;white-space:nowrap">/ m</span>{% endif -%}
